    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d652">

                <pb facs="0843" n="755" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv02/pg755"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">600.119/1912c: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chargé in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Laughlin</hi>)<anchor n="30"
                        xml:id="d652-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-12-14">December 14,
                            1918</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>For Sheldon [from War Trade Board]: No. 1849. We will issue a general license,
                    effective December 16, known as R.A.C. 63, permitting <pb facs="0844" n="756"
                        xml:id="pg756"/> the exportation without the issuance of individual licenses
                    of all commodities not on Conservation List to the United Kingdom, France, Italy
                    and Japan, including their colonies, possessions and protectorates.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d652-f1" n="30" type="source" xml:id="d652-f1-content">
                <p>The same, on same date, to Embassies in France (for McFadden, No. 497), Italy
                    (for Stewart, No. 54), and Japan (for Rabbitt, No. 159).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
